# THE LAWS OF THE DEMIURGE-BLOCKCHAIN
- SERVER: Always refer to the physical server as 'Monad' and hostname as 'Pleroma'.
- IDENTITY: 'Qor ID' is the singular, non-dual identity system for all users.
- CURRENCY: 'Creator God Token' (CGT, since ADR-034). Precision: 18 decimals. The atomic unit is the ember: 1 CGT = 10^18 embers. A Spark is a thousandth of a CGT (10^15 embers), a unit of display and entry, not of the chain (ADR-101). All amounts are integer embers in u128; never floating point; excess precision is rejected, never truncated. Single source of truth for precision: chain/runtime/src/denomination.rs.
- SUPPLY: Base supply 100,000,000,000,000 CGT (one hundred trillion), the large majority allocated at genesis and released over a multi-decade decay curve, plus a small perpetual issuance for infrastructure with fee burn as its counterweight (ADR-003, ADR-004). The fixed 13,000,000,000 supply is superseded. Until the issuance mechanism is built, no code path may create CGT outside --dev.
- ECONOMICS: Defined only by docs/economics/CGT.md and ADR-002 to ADR-008 in docs/decisions/. CGT's value comes from demand to spend it, not to hold it (ADR-002). Every value listed in docs/economics/OPEN_QUESTIONS.md is undecided and must never be invented in code, tests or documents.
- LANGUAGE: Demiurge is infrastructure for creators to earn from use, not a vehicle for appreciation (ADR-008). No APY, yield, return (financial sense), ROI, investment, passive income, or talk of CGT's price or future value, in copy, comments, names or documentation. Earnings are payment for work, hosting and licensing.
- BASE LAYER: Demiurge is a purpose-built Substrate L1 on the Polkadot SDK (ADR-013); the move completed at M3.5. Consensus, finality, networking, storage, transaction validity and runtime upgrades use standard Substrate components; custom pallets are for the creative layer only, and any departure from a standard pallet needs a written reason. chain/ is the only chain in this repository; the custom Rust devnet in framework/ was retired at M3.5 and deleted. No migration code is written until the owner has reviewed docs/architecture/MIGRATION_INVENTORY.md.
- TOOLS: 'Qor Installer' (Setup) and 'Qor Launcher' (The Hub).
- NAMING: Use Gnostic conventions (Aeons, Archons, Syzygies) for internal logic that no outside party reads. Anything that appears in runtime metadata or is published to other developers (crates, pallets and their runtime instance names, calls, events, storage, SDK and RPC surfaces) uses plain, greppable, descriptive names under the Polkadot SDK convention (`pallet-*`), because every wallet and SDK decodes them (ADR-032). Ask for confirmation before naming new modules.
- HARDWARE: All high-entropy operations (Substrate/UE5) must use /data (RAID 0).
- DOCUMENTATION: Only the documents indexed in docs/README.md are current. All pre-realignment documentation was deleted on 2026-09-13 and must NEVER be restored (including from git history) or used for any reason: not as a reference, a source of facts or numbers, an example, or background reading. docs/DIRECTION.md is the only roadmap. docs/DECISIONS.md is the only decision log; it indexes the architecture decision records in docs/decisions/. If a fact is not in a current document, verify it in the code and write it into a current document.
